From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nova <361320585+q2-nova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:35:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Build without MP and P2P, at -Os, with eight TX buffers

Memory headroom on the Q2, measured against the V0.123 kernel build:

- CONFIG_MP_INCLUDED off: the factory test mode (iwpriv mp_*). Text
  -82.5 kB, rodata -12.9 kB.
- CONFIG_P2P off: Wi-Fi Direct. The player runs one station on wlan0.
  Text -79.6 kB.
- -Os instead of -O1. Text -176.5 kB, rodata -11.8 kB.
- NR_XMITBUFF 16 to 8 for SDIO. Each TX buffer is a 20,992-byte kmalloc,
  an order-3 (32 KiB) page block: 256 KiB less per adapter at probe, and
  half the order-3 allocations at each Wi-Fi power-on. Eight buffers hold
  up to 160 KiB of aggregated frames; the player transmits requests and
  TCP acknowledgements.

Together: text 1,519,788 to 1,207,140 bytes, rodata 176,338 to 151,254,
module core 2,032 to 1,696 KiB in pages. AP mode stays: with it off,
core/rtw_csa.c and the CSA action sender in core/rtw_mlme_ext.c do not
build (they use the AP-only rf_ctl_t fields under CONFIG_ECSA). The
/proc/net/rtl8733bs tree (CONFIG_PROC_DEBUG) stays: the player reads
rx_signal, the Wi-Fi script ap_info and the power tools ps_info.
BT_COEXIST unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Makefile           | 6 +++---
 include/rtw_xmit.h | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += $(USER_EXTRA_CFLAGS)
-EXTRA_CFLAGS += -O1
+EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Os
 #EXTRA_CFLAGS += -O3
 #EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wall
 #EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wextra
@@ -71,8 +71,8 @@
 ########################## Features ###########################
 CONFIG_AP_MODE = y
 CONFIG_ECSA = y
-CONFIG_P2P = y
-CONFIG_MP_INCLUDED = y
+CONFIG_P2P = n
+CONFIG_MP_INCLUDED = n
 CONFIG_POWER_SAVING = y
 CONFIG_IPS_MODE = default
 CONFIG_LPS_MODE = default
--- a/include/rtw_xmit.h
+++ b/include/rtw_xmit.h
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
 	#endif
 
 	#if defined CONFIG_SDIO_HCI
-		#define NR_XMITBUFF	(16)
+		#define NR_XMITBUFF	(8)
 		#define SDIO_TX_DIV_NUM (2)
 	#endif
 	#if defined(CONFIG_GSPI_HCI)
-- 
